      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-pure-e/q2-solution-2.svg\" alt=\"The trapezium estimate is π 24[1 + 20.08554 + 2(1.07444 + 1.39561 + 2.71828)] ≈4.118 . [A1] (b) Since sec2 x = 1 + tan2 x, esec2 x = e1+tan2 x = e · etan2 x, so the integrand is e times the one in (a). [B1] Taking the constant outside gives Z π/3 etan2 x dx ≈e(4.118 . . .). e 0 The estimate is 11.19 . [M1] [A1] (c) On this interval tan2 x has positive second derivative. [B1] Its exponential is also strictly convex, so the chords lie above the curve: The ordinates near the right endpoint increase especially rapidly, as the sketch shows: Both estimates are overestimates: [A1] With only four panels and steep growth near the upper limit, the error may be substantial: [A1]\" style=\"--madas-width:680.0px\"></figure>",
