    "steps": [
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-pure-e/q3-solution-1.svg\" alt=\"Suppose p/q + q/p &lt; 2. [B1] Putting both terms over their common denominator gives (p2 + q2)/(pq) &lt; 2. As pq &gt; 0, multiplication gives p2 + q2 &lt; 2pq, [A1] so p2 −2pq + q2 &lt; 0, or (p −q)2 &lt; 0, [A1] a contradiction since the square of a real number is nonnegative: [A1] Therefore p/q + q/p ≥2 . [A1]\" style=\"--madas-width:680.0px\"></figure>",
