      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-pure-e/q7-solution-1.svg\" alt=\"(a) The intercepts of f are (−2a, 0), (0, 2a/3), and those of g are (a/2, 0), (0, a) . [M1] [M1] [M1] [A1] One mark for each of the four correctly located intercepts\" style=\"--madas-width:540.0px\"></figure>",
      "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-pure-e/q7-solution-2.svg\" alt=\"(b) If x ≤a/2, set (x + 2a)/3 = a −2x. [M1] Multiplication by 3 gives x + 2a = 3a −6x, so 7x = a. Substitution gives y = (a/7 + 2a)/3 . = 15a/21 This gives x = a/7, y = 5a/7, [A1] which lies on the correct branch: If x ≥a/2, [A1] set (x + 2a)/3 = 2x −a to obtain x + 2a = 6x −3a. Thus 5x = 5a and y = (a + 2a)/3, giving x = a, y = a. [A1] Thus the points are (a/7, 5a/7) and (a, a) . [A1]\" style=\"--madas-width:660.0px\"></figure>",
