    "question": "<figure class=\"madas-excerpt\"><img src=\"resources/madas/alevel-pure-e/q12-question-1.svg\" alt=\"A curve lies entirely above the x axis and has parametric equations 1 5 x = 2 t , y = , t ≥ 0 . 5 1 + 2 t 2 The finite region R is bounded by the curve, the x axis, the y axis and the straight line with equation x = 2 . ( ) 8 Use integration in parametric to find the exact area of R .\" style=\"--madas-width:573.3px\"></figure>",
